{
  "title": "Dictionary Operations — .get(), keys & Mutation",
  "subtitle": "Safe Lookups and Modifying Dictionaries",
  "topic": "7.2 • DICTIONARY OPERATIONS",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      7.2 • Safe Access & Mutation\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Dictionary <hlt>Methods & Safe Lookups</hlt>\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Accessing a missing key with square brackets throws a <code>KeyError</code> crash. Using <code>.get()</code> ensures rock-solid crash-free programs!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #a7f3d0; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Safe Lookup with .get()\n    </span>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      <code>dict.get(key, default_value)</code> returns the value if the key exists, or the safe default value if missing:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      user = {<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"name\"</span>: <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Alice\"</span>}<br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Safe: returns 'Guest' instead of crashing</span><br/>\n      role = user.get(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"role\"</span>, <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Guest\"</span>)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(role)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: Guest</span><br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Adding a new key</span><br/>\n      user[<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"active\"</span>] = <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">True</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(user)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># {'name': 'Alice', 'active': True}</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}